    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d60">

                <pb facs="0119" n="37" sameAs="frus:frus1945Malta/pg37"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the President
                        </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d60-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-01-17">17 January
                        1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>(Personal and Top Secret for the President from Harriman)</p>
                <p>Reference cable ... [of January 16], White House number 167, in my first talk
                    with Molotov about arrangements I told him I felt sure it would be desirable for
                    you to have your own mess and mess crew and bring your own food for your usual
                    diet just as we had arranged it in Teheran. He readily agreed and I am
                    thoroughly satisfied he took it as an appropriate and quite natural thing to do.
                    I have since been advised that arrangements on this basis are being made in the
                    twenty-one room palace mentioned in my . . . [telegram of January 16].<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d60-f2"/> Weather permitting I expect to go there on the 21st,
                    and have arranged to take Kathleen<anchor n="3" xml:id="d60-f3"/> along as this
                    is her department.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d60-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d60-f1-content">
                <p>Sent by the United States Naval Attaché, Moscow, via Navy channels.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d60-f2" n="2" xml:id="d60-f2-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg36">p. 36</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d60-f3" n="3" xml:id="d60-f3-content">
                <p>Miss Kathleen Harriman.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
